EnD — Beast Box combined runtime/developer kit, 0.4.0

START
Python 3.10–3.12. Create an environment, then install the included wheel:
  python -m venv .venv
  # Activate .venv for your platform.
  python -m pip install cosmos_beast_box-0.4.0-py3-none-any.whl
  python -m beastbox runtime init --data-dir ./my-beast
  python -m beastbox runtime chat "Remember the sunflower code is marigold" --data-dir ./my-beast
  python -m beastbox runtime chat "Recall the sunflower code" --data-dir ./my-beast
  python -m beastbox runtime inspect --data-dir ./my-beast
The source checkout alternative is python -m pip install -e . at repo root.

API
  from beastbox import DurableRuntime
  from beastbox.providers import LocalOllamaProvider
  runtime = DurableRuntime("./my-beast")
  try:
      runtime.respond("remember an owner-provided fact")
      runtime.swap_provider(LocalOllamaProvider(model="YOUR_INSTALLED_MODEL"))
      runtime.respond("recall that fact")
      receipt = runtime.inspect()
  finally:
      runtime.close()

MODEL / CONFIGURATION
Normal reference mode is deterministic software, not a trained model.
For local inference, install/start Ollama and select an existing model:
  python -m beastbox runtime chat "Recall sunflower code" --data-dir ./my-beast --provider ollama --model MODEL_NAME
Use the same directory with MODEL_A, then MODEL_B, then MODEL_A.
--url accepts HTTP(S) loopback only. Redirects and proxy environment variables
are disabled. No IBM credentials. No inference fallback if a chosen model fails.
Durable CLI config is explicit flags: --data-dir, --provider, --model, --url,
--allow-simulated-tool. Environment variables do not grant durable tool authority.
Legacy beastbox.json/BEASTBOX_* settings belong to the older chat/cypher paths.

EVENTS / TOOLS
  python -m beastbox runtime sensor-demo --data-dir ./my-beast
  python -m beastbox runtime tool-demo --data-dir ./my-beast
  python -m beastbox runtime tool-demo --allow-simulated-tool --data-dir ./my-beast
Tool demo uses an explicit deterministic protocol fixture. Only a simulated
numeric position is changed, and only with host enablement. No actuator hardware.
The event API accepts schema sensor-event-v1, source text/synthetic-demo/software-event,
text up to 8192 characters and at most 16 numeric features in [-1, 1].

CONTINUITY / RECOVERY
Every completed turn atomically commits memory, associations, CNS/dyn12 state,
R12 routing state, provenance and a hash-chained checkpoint in runtime.sqlite3.
Use one runtime instance per thread; SQLite serializes independent processes.
Each turn reloads validated latest state. Failed turns roll back. Data directories
are owner-private and local, not shared hostile filesystem sandboxes.
  python -m beastbox runtime backup ./snapshot.sqlite3 --data-dir ./my-beast
Keep the printed SHA-256 separately, then recover into a NEW directory:
  python -m beastbox runtime restore ./snapshot.sqlite3 --sha256 HASH --data-dir ./recovered
  python -m beastbox runtime inspect --data-dir ./recovered
Do not copy a live SQLite main file without WAL. Do not edit checkpoints to repair
corruption. Preserve corrupt copies and restore a known-good CLI backup.
Backups retain only committed turns; no indefinite storage or lossless hardware
failure guarantee. Hashes are not signatures; no protection against a privileged
host rewriting the entire database and all retained receipts. No encryption.

COMBINED SOURCE BOUNDARY
This kit assembles installed interfaces and instructions around the existing
COSMOS runtime, CNS, state families, ReconciliationMemory, Hebbian associations,
RefractiveMemoryRouter, bounded output and continuity adapter. It does not vendor
external projects or invent a separate Synapse OS/HEARTLIGHT implementation.
World knowledge/R12 experiments, GGUF/cypher tooling, bio and IBM research retain
separate documented entry points. Physical actuators and cameras are not included.
Detailed paths/status/origins: ECOSYSTEM_MANIFEST.json in release kit or docs/ in repo.

EVIDENCE
  python -m beastbox runtime verify-swap-receipt historical-swap-002.zip
In a source checkout use evidence/system-closure-001/historical-swap-002.zip.
This verifies the exact published historical receipt, not new weight execution.
The final report specifies original frozen checkpoints, source artifact IDs,
preregistration, failures and descriptive interpretation. Reference A/B labels in
new product smoke tests are interface tests, never substitutes for that experiment.

SECURITY / LIMITS
Model output and memory never grant shell, secret, network, deployment or physical
permissions. Python plugins are trusted host code, not a sandbox. Keep private
information out of prompts unless you intend it to persist locally in plaintext.
The store and checkpoints currently scan retained history; large-store throughput,
retention/compaction and hostile multi-tenant deployment are not validated.
Read LICENSE, TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md and READINESS.json before distribution/deployment.
MODEL ≠ SUBSTRATE. MODEL REPLACEMENT ≠ AUTHORITY TRANSFER.
PERSISTENCE ≠ CONSCIOUSNESS. Preserve every null, failure and historical receipt.
